{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"authorities\":[{\"dependency_id\":\"missing.fc4356b7b5dda202cfa18c37\",\"evidence\":{\"quote\":\"These risks include those arising from erroneous, unauthorised or fraudulent eDDA setup requests and subsequent direct debit transactions (referred to as “eDDA Deposits”).\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u0.2\"},\"needed_for_control\":false,\"title_or_locator\":\"Footnote/source for “eDDA” arrangements (footnote 1; not supplied)\"},{\"dependency_id\":\"missing.8a249b39a6219ee7a14a19cf\",\"evidence\":{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms are reminded of their obligations to maintain proper internal control procedures and adequate financial and operational capabilities to protect their operations and clients from financial loss arising from fraud and other dishonest acts3.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u20.4237\"},\"needed_for_control\":true,\"title_or_locator\":\"Authority cited in footnote 3 concerning internal controls and financial/operational capabilities (not supplied)\"}],\"claims\":[{\"action\":\"issue a circular highlighting risks and setting out risk-assessment and mitigation measures\",\"actor\":\"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)\",\"claim_id\":\"c1\",\"conditions\":[\"Applies to licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers and associated entities using simplified eDDA arrangements for client deposits\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to highlight the risks associated with the increasing use of simplified Electronic Direct Debit Authorisation (eDDA)1 arrangements2 by licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers and associated entities (collectively referred to as “licensed firms”), such as internet brokers and virtual asset trading platform operators, for receiving client deposits. These risks include those arising from erroneous, unauthorised or fraudulent eDDA setup requests and subsequent direct debit transactions (referred to as “eDDA Deposits”). This circular also sets out measures for assessing and mitigating such risks to assist licensed firms in protecting their operations and clients from financial losses.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u0.2\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"SCOPE\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"The SFC circular concerns simplified eDDA arrangements used by specified licensed firms to receive client deposits and addresses associated fraud, authorisation and error risks.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"Footnotes 1 and 2 defining or sourcing eDDA arrangements are not supplied.\"]},{\"action\":\"enable clients to transfer funds from same-name bank accounts to trading accounts through mobile applications or websites\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c2\",\"conditions\":[\"Funds must come from the client's own bank account\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms adopt simplified eDDA arrangements to enable clients to transfer funds from their own bank accounts (ie, same-name accounts) to their trading accounts through licensed firms’ mobile trading applications or trading websites, thereby facilitating a more efficient deposit process for trading or settlement purposes.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u2.834\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"DEFINITION\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"Simplified eDDA arrangements are described as same-name transfers into trading accounts via firm applications or websites.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"obtain pre-authorisation and specified personal and bank-account information\",\"actor\":\"client\",\"claim_id\":\"c3\",\"conditions\":[\"Information is provided through the licensed firm's mobile trading application or trading website\",\"The firm is the payee initiating an eDDA setup request\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(a) a client provides the licensed firm, through the firm’s mobile trading application or trading website, with pre-authorisation and necessary personal and bank account information for the firm, as payee, to initiate an eDDA setup request for withdrawing funds from the client’s designated bank account. Such information generally includes the bank’s name, bank account number, bank account owner’s name, the type of identification document used to open the bank account, and the corresponding identification document number; and\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u4.1272\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The setup process generally requires client pre-authorisation plus bank name, account number, account-owner name, identification-document type and number.\",\"temporal\":[\"During a simplified eDDA setup request\"],\"uncertainty\":[\"The text says information 'generally includes', so the complete required set may vary.\"]},{\"action\":\"submit the setup request and client information to the payee bank for onward transmission to the payer bank\",\"actor\":\"licensed firm\",\"claim_id\":\"c4\",\"conditions\":[\"The payee bank transmits the request and information to the bank maintaining the client's designated account\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(b) the setup request, together with the information provided by the client, is then submitted to the licensed firm’s bank (ie, the payee bank), which further transmits the request and information to the bank at which the client’s designated bank account is maintained (ie, the payer bank) for verification and acceptance.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u5.1804\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The request proceeds from the firm to its payee bank and then to the payer bank for verification and acceptance.\",\"temporal\":[\"After the client supplies setup information\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"confirm the eDDA setup request\",\"actor\":\"bank account owner\",\"claim_id\":\"c5\",\"conditions\":[\"Only where the payer bank's practices and payee/payer-bank arrangements require confirmation\",\"Usually through payer-bank mobile or internet banking\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Subject to the payer bank’s practices and the commercial arrangements between the payee bank and the payer bank, the payer bank may or may not require the bank account owner (ie, the licensed firm’s client as payer) to confirm the eDDA setup request. Where confirmation is required, it is usually conducted through the payer bank’s mobile banking application or internet banking website. The setup process generally takes longer if confirmation is required.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u6.2130\"}],\"exceptions\":[\"Confirmation may not be required.\"],\"kind\":\"EXCEPTION\",\"modality\":\"MAY\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Owner confirmation is conditional on payer-bank practice and commercial arrangements; when required it is generally electronic and lengthens setup.\",\"temporal\":[\"During setup\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"confirm that authorisation from the bank account owner has been obtained\",\"actor\":\"licensed firm\",\"claim_id\":\"c6\",\"conditions\":[\"Bank account owner confirmation is not required\",\"The firm’s bank requires this confirmation\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Where confirmation from the bank account owner is not required, the licensed firm may be required by its bank to confirm that authorisation from the bank account owner has been obtained.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u7.2593\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"MAY\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"If owner confirmation is omitted, the firm's bank may require the firm to attest that owner authorisation was obtained.\",\"temporal\":[\"When confirmation is not required\"],\"uncertainty\":[\"The text does not state which payer/payee-bank configurations impose this requirement.\"]},{\"action\":\"indemnify the payee bank for specified losses or liabilities\",\"actor\":\"licensed firm\",\"claim_id\":\"c7\",\"conditions\":[\"The firm's bank requires an indemnity\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"More importantly, the licensed firm may also be required to indemnify its bank against any losses or liabilities the bank may incur, including third-party claims, arising from the processing of eDDA setup requests or subsequent eDDA Deposits.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u7.2593\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"MAY\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The firm may have to indemnify its bank for losses, liabilities and third-party claims arising from setup requests or deposits.\",\"temporal\":[\"For processing of setup requests and subsequent eDDA Deposits\"],\"uncertainty\":[\"Whether an indemnity is required depends on bank arrangements.\"]},{\"action\":\"ensure proper authorisation from the bank account owner\",\"actor\":\"licensed firm initiating setup and deposits without owner confirmation\",\"claim_id\":\"c8\",\"conditions\":[\"A simplified eDDA setup request is processed without confirmation from the bank account owner\",\"Subsequent eDDA Deposits are initiated at the client's request\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"When a simplified eDDA setup request is processed without confirmation from the bank account owner, the licensed firm that initiates the setup request and subsequent eDDA Deposits at the client’s request bears primary responsibility for ensuring that it has obtained proper authorisation from the bank account owner.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u9.3081\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"MUST\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The initiating firm bears primary responsibility for obtaining proper owner authorisation when no owner confirmation occurs.\",\"temporal\":[\"At setup and for subsequent deposits\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"maintain proper internal controls and adequate financial and operational capabilities\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c9\",\"conditions\":[\"Protection concerns financial loss from fraud and other dishonest acts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms are reminded of their obligations to maintain proper internal control procedures and adequate financial and operational capabilities to protect their operations and clients from financial loss arising from fraud and other dishonest acts3.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u20.4237\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"MUST\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Licensed firms have obligations to maintain internal controls and adequate capabilities against fraud-related losses.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"The cited underlying authority is not supplied.\"]},{\"action\":\"review arrangements, assess risks and implement appropriate mitigation\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms adopting simplified eDDA for client deposits\",\"claim_id\":\"c10\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"In this regard, licensed firms adopting simplified eDDA arrangements for receiving client deposits should review these arrangements, assess the associated risks, and implement appropriate risk mitigating measures.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u20.4237\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Firms should review simplified eDDA arrangements, assess risks and implement mitigation.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"understand arrangements, risk exposures and obligations and review relevant bank contracts\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c11\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms are reminded to have a thorough understanding of simplified eDDA arrangements for receiving client deposits, as well as their related risk exposures and obligations. For example, they should review the relevant service agreements, terms of business and other contractual documents with their banks.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u22.4760\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Firms should understand the arrangements and related exposures/obligations, including by reviewing bank agreements and terms.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"review indemnities\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c12\",\"conditions\":[\"Before entering into or continuing existing simplified eDDA arrangements\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(a) review the terms of any indemnities provided, or to be provided, to their banks;\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u24.5184\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Firms should review existing or proposed bank indemnity terms.\",\"temporal\":[\"Before entering into or continuing arrangements\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"identify eligible payer banks and determine whether owner confirmation is required\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c13\",\"conditions\":[\"Before entering into or continuing existing simplified eDDA arrangements\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(b) identify the payer banks for which their payee banks can facilitate simplified eDDA arrangements, and understand whether such payer banks require confirmation from bank account owners for eDDA setup requests;\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u25.5270\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Firms should identify supported payer banks and their confirmation requirements.\",\"temporal\":[\"Before entering into or continuing arrangements\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"assess risks, operational capability and financial resources\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c14\",\"conditions\":[\"Assessment concerns risks identified from payer-bank confirmation practices\",\"Consider erroneous, unauthorised or fraudulent requests and deposit instructions\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(c) assess the relevant risks arising from (b), including those from erroneous, unauthorised or fraudulent eDDA setup requests and eDDA Deposit instructions, as well as the firms’ operational capabilities to address such risks, having regard to the risk mitigating measures that the firms may adopt, and their financial resources to meet potential claims; and\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u26.5484\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Firms should assess relevant risks, mitigation capacity and resources for potential claims.\",\"temporal\":[\"Before entering into or continuing arrangements\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"review the risk assessment periodically and after material changes\",\"actor\":\"licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c15\",\"conditions\":[\"Material changes concern scale or risk profile\",\"Have regard to listed risk factors\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(d) review the risk assessment in (c) periodically and whenever material changes occur to the scale or risk profile of their simplified eDDA arrangements, having regard to risk factors including those mentioned in paragraph 6.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u27.5845\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"TIME\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Risk assessments should be revisited periodically and whenever arrangement scale or risk profile materially changes.\",\"temporal\":[\"Periodically\",\"Whenever material changes occur\"],\"uncertainty\":[\"Paragraph 6 risk factors are not included in this source piece.\"]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"The supplied piece does not provide footnotes 1–3 or paragraph 6, so definitions and referenced obligations/risk factors remain dependent on missing authorities.\",\"Whether owner confirmation, firm attestation or indemnity is required depends on payer-bank practices and payee/payer-bank commercial arrangements.\",\"The piece describes a typical process; exact information and operational requirements may vary by bank arrangement.\"],\"units\":[{\"claim_ids\":[\"c1\"],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Opening scope and purpose of the SFC circular.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u0.2\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Section heading introducing background.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u1.787\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c2\"],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Defines the purpose and same-name nature of simplified eDDA arrangements.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u2.834\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Introduces the typical setup steps.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u3.1168\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c3\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Client pre-authorisation and identification/account information step.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u4.1272\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c4\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Transmission to payee and payer banks for verification and acceptance.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u5.1804\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c5\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Conditional owner confirmation method and timing effect.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u6.2130\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c6\",\"c7\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Alternative bank-imposed attestation and indemnity requirements when confirmation is absent.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u7.2593\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Section heading introducing risk discussion.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u8.3026\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c8\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Primary responsibility for obtaining authorisation without owner confirmation.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u9.3081\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Risk subheading and lead-in; detailed risk items follow in other units.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u17.3478\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Indemnity and financial-risk examples qualifying the control context.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u18.3802\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Section heading introducing mitigation measures.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u19.4190\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c9\",\"c10\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Internal-control obligation and recommended review, assessment and mitigation.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u20.4237\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Section heading introducing risk assessment.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u21.4708\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c11\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Understanding arrangements and reviewing contractual documents.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u22.4760\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Introduces actions required before entering or continuing arrangements.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u23.5079\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c12\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Review of indemnity terms.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u24.5184\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c13\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Identification of payer banks and confirmation requirements.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u25.5270\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c14\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Risk, capability and financial-resource assessment.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u26.5484\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c15\"],\"disposition\":\"CLAIMS\",\"rationale\":\"Periodic and event-triggered reassessment.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u27.5845\"}]}"}}
